course: dictionary
lesson: 2386
title: Curious: wanting to know, or strange
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Curious has two main meanings. The first is wanting to know or learn about something. «Respect means being curious and kind: asking polite questions» shows that curious means eager to learn, and asking questions is how you show it.
explain: The second meaning is strange or unusual, as in «a curious noise». Use the words around curious to choose the right meaning. «Goats are curious browsers that nibble a bit of everything» tells you goats are keen to explore and test things, so curious means eager to find out here. Ask yourself: is someone wanting to know something, or is something strange?
explain: The noun is curiosity, the feeling of wanting to find out. Being curious is good, and it is how science starts, but stay safe. Do not touch unknown animals, plants, pills or objects. Ask an adult first.
fact: Curious means wanting to know or learn about something.
fact: Curious can also mean strange, unusual or interesting in a surprising way.
fact: Curiosity is the noun: the feeling of wanting to find out.
fact: «Curious about» is followed by the thing you want to know about, as in «curious about stars».
fact: «Curiosity killed the cat» is a saying that warns against being too nosy.
exercise: «Respect means being curious and kind: asking polite questions, and never laughing at someone's food.» Here curious means | Strange and surprising | Bored and tired | Cross and noisy | *Wanting to learn about other people and their ways
exercise: Ella heard a curious noise coming from the attic. What does curious mean here? | Loud and rude | Very tired | Wanting a snack | *Strange and unusual
exercise: Find and copy the noun that means the feeling of wanting to find out. | knowledge | curious | question | *curiosity
test: «Curiosity killed the cat» is a saying that warns against | feeling cold | *being too nosy | losing a game | being too tired
test: Why should you ask an adult before touching an unknown plant? | Because adults like plants more | Because plants are always friendly | Because plants never grow | *Because some plants can be harmful, so being curious needs care
exam: Which sentence uses curious to mean wanting to find out? | The curious bus was late | *Ruby was curious about the stars, so she asked her teacher many questions | The curious noise came from the kitchen | The curious hat was blue and red
